## csb-r1
Execution recipe chosen by Shorted to test the screen; the author's own entries and exits differ.
Buys at the next traded open after the close on which a stock becomes triggered, only when its breakout date has never been traded in this code. Skipped when that open is more than 10% above the captured pivot. After an exit, no re-entry for 10 sessions.
Exits at a close below the captured pivot.
Time stop: exits at the next traded open after the close of session 20 after entry.
Rules are checked at each close in the order listed; the first to hit exits, filled at the next traded open.
A stock with no bar for 20 sessions exits at its last close.
Up to 10 positions, each 10% of equity at the decision close, taken in rank order: highest score first, then code ascending.
Brokerage 10 bps per side, at least A$10 per fill.
Spread and impact per side by 20-session dollar volume at the decision close: A$20,000,000 and over at 5 bps; A$5,000,000 to under A$20,000,000 at 10 bps; A$1,000,000 to under A$5,000,000 at 25 bps; A$250,000 to under A$1,000,000 at 50 bps; under A$250,000 at 75 bps.
Notional at most 5% of the 20-session dollar volume at the decision close.
Total return: adjusted prices per bar, plus cash dividends on their ex-dates (franking excluded).
Short positions are the ones ASIC had published by the decision session.
A delisted stock exits at its last close.
Starting capital A$100,000.
Idle cash earns the RBA cash rate.

## mtt-r1
Execution recipe chosen by Shorted to test the screen; the author's own entries and exits differ.
Buys at the next traded open after the close on which a stock becomes triggered. After an exit, no re-entry for 10 sessions. Buys the session a stock first passes the template; Minervini waits for a volatility-contraction entry we do not detect.
Stop loss: exits at a close at or below 8% under the entry price.
Exits at a close below the 50-day average.
Exits when the status falls to watch or none.
Rules are checked at each close in the order listed; the first to hit exits, filled at the next traded open.
A stock with no bar for 20 sessions exits at its last close.
Up to 10 positions, each 10% of equity at the decision close, taken in rank order: highest score first, then code ascending.
Brokerage 10 bps per side, at least A$10 per fill.
Spread and impact per side by 20-session dollar volume at the decision close: A$20,000,000 and over at 5 bps; A$5,000,000 to under A$20,000,000 at 10 bps; A$1,000,000 to under A$5,000,000 at 25 bps; A$250,000 to under A$1,000,000 at 50 bps; under A$250,000 at 75 bps.
Notional at most 5% of the 20-session dollar volume at the decision close.
Total return: adjusted prices per bar, plus cash dividends on their ex-dates (franking excluded).
Short positions are the ones ASIC had published by the decision session.
A delisted stock exits at its last close.
Starting capital A$100,000.
Idle cash earns the RBA cash rate.

